// codebox_seed.gen -- f_formconstants noise stage: hash noise, deterministic
// per texel per salt. Render-resolution float32 (@adapt 0, `r dim` resize).
// Mirror: tests/modules/formconstants/fc_mirror.seed_state() (the seed
// channels); the per-frame field (the Box-Muller happens downstream in the
// nl stage). Same mechanism as f_wc's codebox_seed.gen, dim-generalized.
//
// Inputs: the first inlet is the `r draw` bang (unused; it only triggers the
// render every frame). Packing: R = seed-E hash, G = seed-I hash (the pass
// stage reads these ONLY on the frame reseed is 1: uniform [0, 1) per field,
// independent channels, never zero), B, A = the two raw uniforms the nl stage
// turns into the per-frame Box-Muller noise (the load-bearing mechanism,
// tasks.md T002).
//   - `salt` increments EVERY FRAME (the `r draw` counter in the raw wiring):
//     the per-frame drive is what sustains the web (T002)
//   - no sin(): a Hoskins-style arithmetic hash (fract and multiply-add only)
//   - scalars only: components are never read from a stored vec
//   - never name a variable e or phi (predefined constants)
//   - functions are declared before Param declarations (GenExpr rule)
hashf(x, y) {
	ha = fract(x * 0.1031);
	hb = fract(y * 0.1031);
	hc = ha;
	hd = ha * (hb + 33.33) + hb * (hc + 33.33) + hc * (ha + 33.33);
	ha = ha + hd;
	hb = hb + hd;
	hc = hc + hd;
	return fract((ha + hb) * hc);
}

Param salt(0);

px = floor(norm.x * dim.x);
py = floor(norm.y * dim.y);

sa = salt * 61;
sb = salt * 17;
se = hashf(px + sa, py + sb);
si = hashf(px + sa + 113.7, py + sb + 57.3);
na = hashf(px + sa + 271.9, py + sb + 181.3);
nb = hashf(px + sa + 401.1, py + sb + 333.7);

out1 = vec(se, si, na, nb);
